{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7b5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d34-fcf0-7332-85e2-0e8a0d37c76e"},"sequence":565,"recorded_at":1780531400001125,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7741b655-4956-456e-8ab0-1e5b6c597882","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"7741b655-4956-456e-8ab0-1e5b6c597882","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7741b655-4956-456e-8ab0-1e5b6c597882"},"call_id":"call_01a07d36d4887680a6958ab545df00c6","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-25-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'schema()' --format json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); ops=d.get('operations',d); import json as j; print(list(ops.keys()) if isinstance(ops,dict) else str(type(ops))[:500])\\\"\\necho \\\"===\\\"\\ntask-board spawn --help 2>&1 | head -n 60\",\n  \"description\": \"List schema operations and spawn help\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"<class 'list'>\\n===\\nQueue an AI agent run (agy, claude, codex, gemini, muse, or qwen) for a board element.\\n\\nspawn.preferred_agentic_system is an optional provider allow-set. exclusive\\npins one provider; mixed retains runtime affinity when it belongs to the set or\\naccepts an explicit in-set --agent. Out-of-set providers are refused before\\ntask lookup or launch side effects. Legacy spawn.preferred_agent retains its\\nbest-effort preference behavior. Runtime affinity detects Codex from\\nCODEX_SESSION, CODEX_THREAD_ID, or CODEX_CI and otherwise selects Claude.\\nOptional spawn.schedule UTC windows temporarily replace the base provider set.\\nA provider or registered model outside the active window is refused before\\nside effects with the allowed set and a concrete retry step; the selected\\nprovider's ceiling is applied afterward.\\n\\nOn launch: assigns element to agent name, sets status from role config and\\nqueues a tracked background RUN. By default the public command returns\\nimmediately with observation commands. Pass --wait to block in the same process\\nuntil the RUN reaches a terminal state; no separate 'task-board spawn wait\\nRUN-...' invocation is needed. The --background flag is required so execution placement is explicit\\nat every callsite.\\n\\nPrompt composition:\\n  Primary source of truth is the board:\\n    - Task description comes from the element README\\n    - Task-specific DoD comes from the element checklist\\n    - Instructions come from precondition resources attached to the element\\n\\n  Legacy compatibility overrides:\\n    --task-path FILE  Optional extra brief appended to the task description\\n    --dod-path FILE   Optional extra DoD lines appended to the prompt only\\n\\nThe prompt is always composed from the role template plus board state. Legacy\\nfile overrides only append extra context — they never replace role identity,\\nboard task context, FIRST/LAST status blocks, skills, or CLI reference.\\n\\nSafety:\\n  --instruction NAME  Validates that a precondition resource matching NAME\\n                      is linked to the task before spawning. Errors with a\\n                      helpful message if not found.\\n\\nPrompt file is auto-saved to .temp/prompts/ with timestamp naming.\\n\\nModel and reasoning selection:\\n  --model is required for every spawn of a role without a configured default.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Codex spawns.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Qwen spawns.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Claude spawns, except claude-haiku-4-5\\n  (and its dated snapshot), which take no effort at all.\\n  task-board never supplies model or reasoning defaults of its own. The only\\n  exception is a per-role default the project configured explicitly at\\n  spawn.ceilings.<provider>.roles.<role>.default_model and\\n  .default_reasoning_effort. That seed fills only the dimensions omitted at the\\n  callsite, an explicit flag always wins per dimension, and the seeded pair\\n  still passes the ordinary ceiling, so a default can never widen a bound. A\\n  role with no configured default keeps explicit selection mandatory. Inspect\\n  what a role resolves to before spawning with:\\n    task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER)'\\n  Inspect the current registry with: task-board q 'models(agent=codex)'\\n\\n  With model_criterion less_or_equal or greater_or_equal, every spawn also\\n  requires --selection-rationale with one non-empty line explaining the chosen\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3411,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 853,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
